<speak>
<s>This is your briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">31052026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="95%">
<s>American forces fired a missile into the engine room of a Gambia-flagged cargo ship that ignored more than twenty warnings while trying to reach an Iranian port.</s> <s>It's the first live-fire stop under the blockade Washington declared on the seventeenth of April, even as President Trump publicly suggests he may lift the siege.</s> <s>The gap between the announcement and the missile is the real story... and every hull now transiting the Gulf prices in that risk.</s>
</prosody>
<p>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>A single provision buried in the United States House defence bill, Section two-twenty-four, would permanently fuse American and Israeli military research, artificial intelligence, cyber, and data-fusion programmes.</s> <s>It replaces the annual, publicly-voted aid debate with statutory machinery that runs on autopilot — just as polling shows only sixteen percent of Americans back unconditional arms to Israel.</s> <s>The Senate must still clear the text, and whether anyone forces a vote on it remains unsettled.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Australia has quietly abandoned its plan to buy new nuclear submarines and will instead take ageing, secondhand Virginia-class hulls from the United States.</s> <s>American shipyards build just over one such boat a year, while the AUKUS pact needs more than two, and Canberra's own sovereign fleet isn't due until twenty forty-two.</s> <s>It's a downgrade of the promise sold to the public, and Australia must now stretch its thirty-year-old Collins-class boats another decade.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>In Nigeria, Oyo State governor Seyi Makinde has accepted the Allied People's Movement's nomination for the twenty twenty-seven presidential race.</s> <s>His third-party run, backed by all thirty-six state chapters, challenges the two-party grip that's dominated Nigerian politics, on a platform of security decentralisation and oil-company reform.</s> <s>Whether insecurity — the banditry and kidnappings he names — becomes the defining issue of the race is now an open contest.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A drone struck the turbine hall of the Zaporizhzhia nuclear plant in occupied Ukraine, breaching a wall though primary equipment survived.</s> <s>Russia has held the site since twenty twenty-two, its six reactors in cold shutdown, with off-site power already severed sixteen times according to the UN atomic agency.</s> <s>Kyiv denied the strike, and inspectors warn that combat this close to reactor machinery leaves almost no margin for error.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Tom Barrack, the billionaire investor and Trump confidant, has let his formal Syria envoy title lapse, yet keeps central control over Syria, Iraq, and Turkey policy.</s> <s>No successor's been named, so reconstruction, sanctions relief, and the Kurdish file now run through a presidential intimate operating outside the State Department.</s> <s>How that policy is staffed will shape how much room Ankara and Tehran have to maneuver in the post-Assad window.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>India has revised its export duties on petrol, diesel, and jet fuel from the first of June, raising the levies to keep refined fuel at home.</s> <s>New Delhi adjusts these rates every fortnight against crude benchmarks, using export taxes as a lever to ration its refiners' overseas sales and protect local pump prices.</s> <s>The next reset falls in mid-June, and it ripples straight into the wider Asian fuel trade.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Namibia has hired the trading house Vitol to guarantee its fuel supply through September, an emergency measure after Iran's Gulf disruption.</s> <s>African importers with no storage buffer absorbed that shock directly, and Vitol offered the basic fuel price with no premium and no public money, the energy minister said.</s> <s>It's a stopgap that exposes how thin the continent's fuel security really is when distant waterways close.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Bulgaria's budget deficit already breaches the eurozone ceiling, with the European Commission forecasting a gap of four-point-one percent of output this year.</s> <s>Prime Minister Radev says the previous government cut state-controlled prices to squeeze under the inflation threshold for euro entry, a one-time trick that's now unwinding.</s> <s>The formal report publishes on the third of June, and a failure could complicate Sofia's path into the single currency.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Britain's health secretary, Wes Streeting, has endorsed new North Sea oil licences, openly contradicting Labour's twenty twenty-four manifesto.</s> <s>He paired the call with a National Insurance cut and a three-thousand-pound grant for every firm that hires a young, long-term benefit claimant — a pitch that reads as leadership positioning against Keir Starmer.</s> <s>Energy secretary Ed Miliband must now rule on the contested Jackdaw field, with Reform UK shaping the terms of the fight.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Tonight a rare blue moon rises — the second full moon in a single calendar month, and this one also a micromoon at its farthest point from Earth.</s> <s>Sitting two-hundred-fifty-two thousand miles away at apogee, it'll appear six percent smaller and ten percent dimmer, a quirk of the Moon's elliptical orbit that recurs every two to three years.</s> <s>Southern Hemisphere watchers will see it glide in front of the bright star Antares, with peak near nine in the morning, universal time.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Forty isolated fossil teeth unearthed at Algora in central Spain place a fearsome African predator lineage in Cretaceous Europe.</s> <s>Cladistic analysis matched them to majungasaurine abelisaurids, a family best known from Madagascar, showing how isolated teeth alone can let paleontologists pin a whole lineage to a continent.</s> <s>The find leaves the route open — whether these southern predators crossed land bridges along the ancient Tethyan shoreline.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Researchers in Leiden have traced severe multiple sclerosis to immune cells in the brain that become clogged with fat.</s> <s>Microglia normally clear away damaged myelin, but in severe cases they switch from repair to driving the very inflammation that worsens the disease.</s> <s>Blocking a single overactive enzyme improved tissue health in their tests, hinting, God willing, at a new line of treatment.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>The renewed race to the Moon, between China and the United States, isn't really about footprints — it's about oxygen.</s> <s>Both powers are targeting permanent bases, and hauling oxygen up out of Earth's deep gravity well dominates the mass and cost of every mission, so extracting it from lunar soil becomes the enabling technology.</s> <s>Whoever first splits oxygen from the regolith changes the economics of staying — and whoever builds the base sets the rules.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A proposed amendment to the XRP Ledger aims to structurally block flash-loan attacks that have drained decentralised finance of hundreds of millions of dollars.</s> <s>A flash loan borrows millions, executes a price manipulation, and repays it all inside one transaction, putting no real capital at risk — a recurring exploit on Ethereum-style systems.</s> <s>The XRPL design forecloses that move by forbidding such intra-transaction calls, the tradeoff being shallower liquidity.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Physicists at Cornell have watched surface chemistry switch off the electron layer that makes gallium nitride chips work.</s> <s>That two-dimensional electron gas powers the fast chargers in your pocket, and momentum-space imaging revealed exactly how stray surface molecules can quench it or restore it.</s> <s>The map of which treatments preserve that layer points the way toward the next generation of power electronics.</s>
</p>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="90%">
<s>That's your briefing.</s>
</prosody>
</speak>